---
import BackLink from '../components/BackLink.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SOURCE_URL } from '../lib/config';
---

<Layout title="Privacy · Grade Viewer" description="How Grade Viewer handles StudentVUE logins and grades.">
	<main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 pb-16">
		<div class="-ml-1 flex items-center gap-1">
			<BackLink href="/" label="Back to sign in" />
			<h1 class="text-xl font-medium">Privacy</h1>
		</div>
		<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated August 23, 2026</p>

		<div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			<p>
				Grade Viewer is a small educational helper for looking at the grades your school already
				stores in StudentVUE. It is not a district system, and it is not affiliated with,
				endorsed by, or associated with Edupoint, StudentVUE, Synergy, or any school district. It
				is not used for profit, and it is not a place where we collect or keep student records.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">What this app does</h2>
			<p>
				When you sign in, this site sends your StudentVUE username and password to your district’s
				StudentVUE server and asks it for your gradebook, documents, mail, and attendance. The reply is shown to you in the browser.
				The server in the middle exists only so the app can talk to StudentVUE. We do not use your
				login to change anything in the district system, and hypothetical / what-if scores never
				leave this device.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">What we don’t keep</h2>
			<ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
				<li>We do not create accounts, mailing lists, or a database of students.</li>
				<li>We do not save your password or grades in a file, database, or backup that we review.</li>
				<li>We do not sell, share, or look through your gradebook, documents, mail, or attendance.</li>
				<li>We do not send what-if scores, assignment edits, or “needed score” experiments back to
					StudentVUE or to anyone else.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">What stays on your device</h2>
			<p>
				After you sign in once, this browser stores an encrypted copy of your StudentVUE login so
				you don’t have to type your password again. The encryption key never leaves this device, and
				Grade Viewer does not keep a server-side session or cookie with your credentials. Signing
				out deletes the saved login. Charts, filters, and hypothetical assignments exist only in
				that browser tab until you leave.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">Who actually has your grades</h2>
			<p>
				Your school and StudentVUE (Edupoint) already have your grades. Their privacy rules still
				apply. Grade Viewer does not replace those systems; it only displays what they return when
				you sign in.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">Terms of use</h2>
			<p>
				By signing in, you agree to these terms. Grade Viewer is an independent educational
				project. It is not affiliated with Edupoint Educational Systems, StudentVUE, Synergy, or
				any school district. Those names and marks belong to their owners.
			</p>
			<p>
				This site is for educational purposes only. It is not used for profit in any way: there
				are no ads, paid plans, or sale of student data. You may use it only with your own
				StudentVUE account, and you are responsible for following your district’s acceptable-use
				rules.
			</p>
			<p>
				The app is provided “as is,” without warranties of any kind, including accuracy,
				availability, or fitness for a particular purpose. Grades shown here may be incomplete or
				out of date compared with StudentVUE. Grade Viewer and its operators are not liable for
				missed work, incorrect displayed grades, account problems, school or district action, or
				any other loss from using this tool. You use it at your own risk.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">Open source</h2>
			<p>
				Grade Viewer is proudly open source. You can read the code at
				{' '}<a class="underline" href={SOURCE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{SOURCE_URL.replace('https://', '')}</a>
				{' '}and see how sign-in and gradebook requests work.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">Hosting</h2>
			<p>
				The site is hosted on infrastructure that delivers the app and relays those StudentVUE
				requests. Standard web logs from a host (such as the fact that a page was requested) may
				exist on that platform. We do not use that to identify students or read gradebooks.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">Questions</h2>
			<p>
				If you did not mean to use this tool, sign out. That clears the encrypted login on this
				device. You can also close the tab. Nothing is stored for us to delete later, because we do
				not keep a copy.
			</p>
			<p>
				For feedback, problems, or other questions, email
				{' '}<a class="underline" href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</main>
</Layout>
